# Where an effect may be declared, and what it owes.
#
#   * `//platform/effect/beep` declares `Beep`. Its testing surface declares
#     an effect of its own, which only an effect package's production code
#     may, and implements nothing, so `Beep` has no test implementation. The
#     platform's `HostBeep` implements it, which doesn't count.
#   * `//platform/effect/hum` has no `testing` block at all, so `Hum` has no
#     test implementation anywhere.
#   * `//lib/tools` declares an effect in a source under `testing/`, which
#     isn't an effect package either, and has a `platform.buri` that is only a
#     library file, where a function needs a body.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs.

doc: "an effect is declared only in an effect package's production code, and each one has a test implementation in its own testing surface"

run {
  args: ["lint", "//..."]
  exit: 1
  golden: "lint.txt"
}
